nly split state.", "watch": "Republican-sponsored surveys show a single-digit race, so a strong debate week for James or a late national shift toward the GOP could tighten the contest.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Open seat: Gretchen Whitmer (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's governorship is open as Gretchen Whitmer is term-limited, pitting Democrat Jocelyn Benson against Republican John James. The state sits at even partisan lean, but September polling consistently favors Benson: independent pollsters show her ahead by five to twelve points, while Republican-sponsored surveys show a narrower three-to-four point race. Aggregated averages in late September put the lead near seven to nine points.\n\nBenson has raised roughly twice as much money as James and holds a large cash-on-hand advantage, and reporting notes James faces an advertising-spending deficit. Barack Obama campaigned with Benson in early October, and the race has drawn heavy debate attention. Analysts rate the contest Lean Democratic, with one rating it Likely Democratic, and prediction markets price a Benson win around 90 percent or higher. James, seeking to become Michigan's first Black governor, remains a well-known challenger, but the evidence points to a clear Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9339, "margin": 7.39}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9166, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9224, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9193, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8901, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9053, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.911, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9221, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9131, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9322, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.912, "margin": 6.8}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9194, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p